WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
A Greek king in north-west India
meets a Buddhist monk named Nagasena.

2
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.650
The monk asks how the king came.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.830
By chariot, says the king.

4
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.000
So the monk asks: is the pole the chariot?

5
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:13.580
The axle?

6
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.740
The wheels?

7
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.300
The reins?

8
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.930
Now think about you.

9
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.690
Your body, your thoughts and
your moods keep changing.

10
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.870
So if every part of you keeps changing,
is there a you that stays the same?

11
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.950
In this mission, you'll meet three marks
that Buddhists say belong to everything

12
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.130
conditioned.

13
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.230
Then you'll take the chariot
apart, piece by piece,

14
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.530
and see what the monk was driving at.

15
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.620
Your mission: find out
whether, for Buddhists,

16
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.530
any part of you stays the same.
